5.2 Shared step vocabulary
Eleven step kinds cover all five subtypes. A step kind is a Go handler plus a compensation; nothing else in the service may perform a side effect.

Step kind	Does	Compensation
validate_request	Structural + instrument-shape validation, duplicate detection, amount bounds.	None (no side effect)
match_transactions	Pulls posted card transactions in window, applies the MCC/date rule pack, reserves matched rows.	Release matched rows
verify_instrument	Confirms the destination is usable: external account verification, address validation, card status.	None
check_eligibility	One gRPC call to eligibility-svc with the subtype rule pack; snapshots the decision.	None
place_hold	Ledger hold for the points amount, via ledger gateway.	release_hold
submit_disbursement	Rail adapter Submit. Intent row written before the call.	void_disbursement where the rail permits
await_rail_confirmation	Parks the run until an ingested callback or a scheduled poll resolves the rail state.	Stop waiting; escalate
settle_hold	Converts the hold to a permanent points debit.	None — past this point only reverse
notify_member	Emits the notification event (owned by the notification platform).	None
watch_reversal_window	Keeps the order observable for its return window; closes it on expiry.	None
reverse	Restores points and records the claw-back after settlement.	Terminal
