8.2 Idempotency contract
Case	Behaviour
Same key, same body	200 with the stored response. No new order.
Same key, different body	422 idempotency_key_reuse. Fingerprint mismatch is a client bug, not a retry.
Concurrent duplicate	One wins on uq_cr_idem; the loser reads and returns the winner's response.
No key supplied	400. Money-moving commands are never accepted without one.
Internal side effects	Deterministic key: hash(redemptionID, stepSeq, stepKind) — no attempt counter, so every retry presents the identical key to the ledger and the rail.
8.3 Published event
One event type carries the cross-channel status contract. It is deliberately identical in shape to what Gift Card, Shop with Points and Miles publish — that shared shape is the only thing that keeps a choreographed estate coherent, and it is what makes a later move to a shared engine additive rather than a rewrite.

{
  "eventId": "evt_01HZ...",              // consumer dedupe key
